WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.855
- What's up Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:04.855 --> 00:00:07.455
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:07.455 --> 00:00:09.065
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:09.065 --> 00:00:12.473
And my sincere hope is
that if you see in you

00:00:12.473 --> 00:00:15.772
what I see in you you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:15.772 --> 00:00:17.729
So to help you on your journey
today I'm going to talk about

00:00:17.729 --> 00:00:21.896
the seven ways to convince
people to buy your product.

00:00:24.361 --> 00:00:25.441
- [Narrator] Nine,

00:00:25.441 --> 00:00:26.274
eight,

00:00:26.274 --> 00:00:27.126
seven.

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:28.690
(hip hop music)

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:29.537
Seven.

00:00:29.537 --> 00:00:31.376
- So one of the most common
challenges for entrepreneurs

00:00:31.376 --> 00:00:33.523
is we've got a great
product or service to sell

00:00:33.523 --> 00:00:35.524
and we've got to get
out there and sell it.

00:00:35.524 --> 00:00:37.349
How do you convince people that they

00:00:37.349 --> 00:00:39.059
need to buy your thing?

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:41.809
I'm going to give you my seven tips.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.393
Tip number one is to change your mindset.

00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:48.842
I'm not from the old
school sales philosophy

00:00:48.842 --> 00:00:51.651
where you see that next
person coming in as your

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.528
next suit, or as your next car,

00:00:53.528 --> 00:00:55.101
or hitting your next bonus.

00:00:55.101 --> 00:00:57.702
From my perspective
what's really important is

00:00:57.702 --> 00:00:59.098
you're trying to serve them.

00:00:59.098 --> 00:01:00.861
You're trying to actually help this person

00:01:00.861 --> 00:01:01.943
make a good decision.

00:01:01.943 --> 00:01:04.064
That may mean pushing them a little bit,

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.175
that may mean once you understand them

00:01:06.175 --> 00:01:07.814
to give them the best solution.

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:09.000
And we'll go through the points.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.525
But it starts with the mindset
of you are there to serve,

00:01:11.525 --> 00:01:14.604
you are there to help and
not just try to close.

00:01:14.604 --> 00:01:17.080
I'm not trying to convince
anybody of anything.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.135
I want to help the person
coming through the door.

00:01:19.135 --> 00:01:20.335
And if you start with that approach

00:01:20.335 --> 00:01:22.515
I think every other step
becomes a lot easier.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.767
The reason why it's so
important is because

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.860
you can spend so much of
your time dealing with people

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.078
who are not good fits for your business.

00:01:30.078 --> 00:01:31.990
A lot of people, a lot
of you guys, if you have

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.658
a list of potential leads or prospects,

00:01:33.658 --> 00:01:36.206
a lot of these people
will never buy from you.

00:01:36.206 --> 00:01:38.592
And you either spend your
time trying to convince

00:01:38.592 --> 00:01:40.878
the people who are not
fits for your company

00:01:40.878 --> 00:01:42.096
to buy from you.

00:01:42.096 --> 00:01:44.236
And it's a long, slow, painful,

00:01:44.236 --> 00:01:46.341
awkward process for both of you.

00:01:46.341 --> 00:01:49.218
Or you abandon that person
and you use that time

00:01:49.218 --> 00:01:51.201
to focus on finding people who are good

00:01:51.201 --> 00:01:52.528
fits for your business.

00:01:52.528 --> 00:01:55.790
And so spend less time
trying to convince everybody

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.376
and more time finding
and helping the people

00:01:58.376 --> 00:01:59.793
who you can help.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.322
Step number two is to listen to them.

00:02:05.322 --> 00:02:09.019
The best tool that you have
as a salesperson is your ears.

00:02:09.019 --> 00:02:10.734
There's a common saying
of there's a reason

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:12.537
why you have two ears and one mouth.

00:02:12.537 --> 00:02:14.371
You need to be able to
listen to your customers,

00:02:14.371 --> 00:02:16.724
to understand what they're looking for.

00:02:16.724 --> 00:02:19.005
The worst salesperson and
you can even experience

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.008
it whatever you're going
to go out and buy at

00:02:21.008 --> 00:02:22.622
if your deal with the salesperson is

00:02:22.622 --> 00:02:24.398
they're just talking at
you, talking, talking,

00:02:24.398 --> 00:02:25.776
talking, talking, talking.

00:02:25.776 --> 00:02:27.694
You're probably going to
get one, really annoyed.

00:02:27.694 --> 00:02:29.656
And two, a lot of what they're saying

00:02:29.656 --> 00:02:30.890
is not going to help you.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.996
And so if you want to switch
that if you want to be

00:02:32.996 --> 00:02:35.553
a great salesperson your
first step is to listen

00:02:35.553 --> 00:02:36.998
to what the people are saying.

00:02:36.998 --> 00:02:38.416
Listen to what their problems are.

00:02:38.416 --> 00:02:41.876
Listen to try to find
points that you understand

00:02:41.876 --> 00:02:43.717
their challenge and then it's easy

00:02:43.717 --> 00:02:45.692
to come up with a solution
that will help them.

00:02:45.692 --> 00:02:48.206
Also as people are talking it helps them

00:02:48.206 --> 00:02:50.201
to feel a little bit more understood

00:02:50.201 --> 00:02:54.284
which improves your sales
process cycle, as well.

00:02:56.686 --> 00:02:58.498
Tip number three is understand their why.

00:02:58.498 --> 00:03:01.988
This is always a really important process

00:03:01.988 --> 00:03:04.488
and one where a lot of
sales people fall down.

00:03:04.488 --> 00:03:07.371
Because people come in
with one reason for why

00:03:07.371 --> 00:03:08.825
they think they're buying from you.

00:03:08.825 --> 00:03:09.806
Or why they think they're interested.

00:03:09.806 --> 00:03:11.578
But there's always a deeper reason

00:03:11.578 --> 00:03:13.395
which they may acknowledge
or they may need a

00:03:13.395 --> 00:03:15.516
couple probing questions to figure out.

00:03:15.516 --> 00:03:18.813
So as an example, people
come to dance here, right.

00:03:18.813 --> 00:03:20.346
Stronger Than Salsa, one of the largest

00:03:20.346 --> 00:03:22.522
dance school for salsa in Canada for sure,

00:03:22.522 --> 00:03:23.619
maybe North America.

00:03:23.619 --> 00:03:25.178
Why do people come here?

00:03:25.178 --> 00:03:26.930
When you ask them at the
beginning it's, well I want

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.200
to learn some steps, I want to you know

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.428
I thought salsa was interesting.

00:03:31.428 --> 00:03:32.770
I want to come and learn.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.565
And it's a very surface level answer,

00:03:34.565 --> 00:03:37.250
it doesn't give me anything.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.748
If I'm trying to sell this person,

00:03:38.748 --> 00:03:40.383
if I'm trying to help this person

00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:42.263
make a decision as to which class might

00:03:42.263 --> 00:03:43.628
be a right fit or even if our school is

00:03:43.628 --> 00:03:45.584
a good fit for them or not,

00:03:45.584 --> 00:03:47.647
I need to understand why
they're coming here, right?

00:03:47.647 --> 00:03:49.784
So as an example, if what
they all they care about

00:03:49.784 --> 00:03:52.177
is the steps and and
their goal is to perform

00:03:52.177 --> 00:03:53.736
and they want to be one of
the world's greatest salsa

00:03:53.736 --> 00:03:56.299
dancers, I'm not going to
sell them on a group class

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:57.673
because you learn more slowly.

00:03:57.673 --> 00:03:59.670
Maybe they want to do private
lessons with an instructor

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.071
to learn as quickly as possible.

00:04:02.071 --> 00:04:04.067
Most people though what
they do is they come

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:05.929
and they want to meet people.

00:04:05.929 --> 00:04:07.263
Maybe they just broke up with somebody

00:04:07.263 --> 00:04:08.800
and they want to get
into a new relationship.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.084
Maybe they just moved to the city

00:04:10.084 --> 00:04:11.458
and they want to make new friends.

00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:13.665
Maybe they're not happy with their work

00:04:13.665 --> 00:04:15.782
and they just need an escape to go.

00:04:15.782 --> 00:04:18.674
Maybe they haven't made any
friends since University

00:04:18.674 --> 00:04:20.254
and the people at their
work they don't really like.

00:04:20.254 --> 00:04:22.276
Or they're an entrepreneur
and they work by themselves

00:04:22.276 --> 00:04:24.271
and they want to come
and meet people, right.

00:04:24.271 --> 00:04:27.181
If that's the incentive to
want to join, that's good

00:04:27.181 --> 00:04:29.194
(mumbling) because when
I'm done talking to them

00:04:29.194 --> 00:04:31.713
I can frame everything in a situation

00:04:31.713 --> 00:04:34.046
that really helps them best.

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:38.415
And so you have to understand
the why behind the why.

00:04:38.415 --> 00:04:40.305
Usually it's not the first
answer but it's the second

00:04:40.305 --> 00:04:41.385
or the third answer.

00:04:41.385 --> 00:04:43.951
So when you ask them why did you find us,

00:04:43.951 --> 00:04:45.151
what inspired you to call,

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.803
what inspired you to come into my store,

00:04:46.803 --> 00:04:49.593
what inspired you to send me that email

00:04:49.593 --> 00:04:51.876
ask one-level why at least deeper

00:04:51.876 --> 00:04:54.035
after you get that first response.

00:04:54.035 --> 00:04:56.044
Because almost by default and
this is when you're dealing

00:04:56.044 --> 00:04:57.468
with a team member this is
when you're dealing with

00:04:57.468 --> 00:04:59.606
investors, when you deal with media

00:04:59.606 --> 00:05:01.346
there's always a why behind the why.

00:05:01.346 --> 00:05:04.008
So ask the why and then when
they give you a response

00:05:04.008 --> 00:05:06.245
ask a second why or third why underneath

00:05:06.245 --> 00:05:07.711
to get to the real core.

00:05:07.711 --> 00:05:09.542
Because if you understand
what really moves them

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.665
you understand the true
intention behind it.

00:05:11.665 --> 00:05:13.811
And probing them a little
bit to figure that out

00:05:13.811 --> 00:05:15.490
you have a much better chance

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.657
of giving them the best
option and closing that sale.

00:05:21.537 --> 00:05:23.453
Tip number four is make a connection.

00:05:23.453 --> 00:05:26.021
At the beginning of this
process there's always this kind

00:05:26.021 --> 00:05:26.854
of standoff right.

00:05:26.854 --> 00:05:28.220
Nobody likes to be sold.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.548
Nobody likes being sold to.

00:05:29.548 --> 00:05:31.303
People like the buy but they
don't like being sold to.

00:05:31.303 --> 00:05:33.846
And so whenever a salesperson
comes up to somebody

00:05:33.846 --> 00:05:36.956
immediately like you tighten
up, you hold in your breath,

00:05:36.956 --> 00:05:38.508
you don't want to reveal too much,

00:05:38.508 --> 00:05:39.979
you don't want to be hard pressure sold.

00:05:39.979 --> 00:05:42.343
That's a typical reaction
that happens a lot.

00:05:42.343 --> 00:05:43.672
But they do want information,

00:05:43.672 --> 00:05:45.141
they do want somebody to help them.

00:05:45.141 --> 00:05:47.609
And so by figuring out their why right

00:05:47.609 --> 00:05:49.305
the why behind the why,

00:05:49.305 --> 00:05:50.851
the next step that you want to do is

00:05:50.851 --> 00:05:53.483
make a personal connection
with them somehow.

00:05:53.483 --> 00:05:56.054
Show them that you understand their why.

00:05:56.054 --> 00:05:57.776
So if you if they're
talking about wanting to

00:05:57.776 --> 00:05:59.173
come take a dance class because they

00:05:59.173 --> 00:06:00.540
want to make new friends,

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.975
because they haven't made any
friends since college right.

00:06:02.975 --> 00:06:05.492
Or if they are trying to
get into relationship,

00:06:05.492 --> 00:06:07.069
they're hoping to meet somebody because

00:06:07.069 --> 00:06:08.451
they just broke up with somebody

00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:12.068
try to hear a personal
story that relates to them.

00:06:12.068 --> 00:06:14.230
So sharing a good personal story, one,

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:15.856
shows that you listen to them.

00:06:15.856 --> 00:06:17.995
One, shows that you
are understanding them.

00:06:17.995 --> 00:06:21.749
And then also shows that
you have a solution for them

00:06:21.749 --> 00:06:23.639
because you've gone through it yourself.

00:06:23.639 --> 00:06:26.673
Because you know what
situation they're in,

00:06:26.673 --> 00:06:29.337
you've come through it and
now I'm going to show you

00:06:29.337 --> 00:06:30.418
the path to do it yourself.

00:06:30.418 --> 00:06:32.873
And so if someone was talking
like that as an example

00:06:32.873 --> 00:06:34.564
I would share about all
the great friendships

00:06:34.564 --> 00:06:36.741
that I've made through dancing.

00:06:36.741 --> 00:06:38.608
How my social circle exploded

00:06:38.608 --> 00:06:40.741
because I took dance classes became part

00:06:40.741 --> 00:06:41.886
of the salsa community.

00:06:41.886 --> 00:06:43.895
That's one of the most
friendly communities, I think,

00:06:43.895 --> 00:06:44.728
in the world.

00:06:44.728 --> 00:06:46.335
I did ballroom dancing,
didn't meet anybody.

00:06:46.335 --> 00:06:49.014
I took salsa, my friend circle exploded.

00:06:49.014 --> 00:06:50.315
I then met my wife.

00:06:50.315 --> 00:06:52.388
If you're talking
relationships I met my wife

00:06:52.388 --> 00:06:53.818
through a salsa dancing.

00:06:53.818 --> 00:06:55.858
It's a great way to be
able to meet people because

00:06:55.858 --> 00:06:59.240
you're in a dance class and
you're rotating partners

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.636
every couple minutes so you get to know

00:07:00.636 --> 00:07:03.568
all the members of the
opposite sex in your class.

00:07:03.568 --> 00:07:05.875
And when you go out to socials and parties

00:07:05.875 --> 00:07:07.477
part of the process is you're dancing

00:07:07.477 --> 00:07:08.681
with lots of different people.

00:07:08.681 --> 00:07:10.716
You don't just stick with
one partner all night

00:07:10.716 --> 00:07:13.095
you're dancing with 20, 30, 40

00:07:13.095 --> 00:07:15.473
different people from the
opposite sex in one night.

00:07:15.473 --> 00:07:17.359
And so friendships just naturally happen,

00:07:17.359 --> 00:07:18.762
relationships just naturally happen.

00:07:18.762 --> 00:07:20.434
And I can share my story.

00:07:20.434 --> 00:07:21.817
And so if I understand that

00:07:21.817 --> 00:07:23.273
that's your real why behind the why

00:07:23.273 --> 00:07:25.556
and then I share with
you my personal story

00:07:25.556 --> 00:07:27.881
not as a sales pitch
to try to convince you

00:07:27.881 --> 00:07:31.980
but a deep understanding
of I am I acknowledge

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:33.472
this fear that you have,

00:07:33.472 --> 00:07:34.576
and this pain that you have,

00:07:34.576 --> 00:07:35.880
and this desire you have.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.102
And then here's how I solved it

00:07:38.102 --> 00:07:40.954
then it's much easier
to get them to follow

00:07:40.954 --> 00:07:41.988
that path with you.

00:07:41.988 --> 00:07:43.641
You disarm them, they feel like they're

00:07:43.641 --> 00:07:45.699
not being sold anymore but you're actually

00:07:45.699 --> 00:07:47.366
trying to help them.

00:07:49.962 --> 00:07:52.979
Tip number five is recommend
a solution that fits.

00:07:52.979 --> 00:07:55.441
And so once you've asked
the why behind the why

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:57.034
and once you've made
that connection with them

00:07:57.034 --> 00:07:59.727
then you have to think,
okay, I now really know

00:07:59.727 --> 00:08:01.385
what this person wants and
I know why they want it.

00:08:01.385 --> 00:08:03.435
Now I need to figure out what's the best

00:08:03.435 --> 00:08:06.422
option for me to be able
to give that person.

00:08:06.422 --> 00:08:08.646
Well try to dance salsa, we
have lots of different classes.

00:08:08.646 --> 00:08:10.607
We have lots of different
options we have salsa,

00:08:10.607 --> 00:08:13.043
we have bachata, we
have performance groups,

00:08:13.043 --> 00:08:14.389
we have private lessons.

00:08:14.389 --> 00:08:15.679
We have lots of different things

00:08:15.679 --> 00:08:16.983
that you could potentially do.

00:08:16.983 --> 00:08:19.211
And as I'm talking to somebody
you know we'll be listening

00:08:19.211 --> 00:08:22.222
okay, here's what they need,
here's what they're asking for.

00:08:22.222 --> 00:08:23.862
That's an X, that's a yes.

00:08:23.862 --> 00:08:26.223
And in some cases and this is this is bold

00:08:26.223 --> 00:08:28.266
but this earns a lot of trust it may mean

00:08:28.266 --> 00:08:31.651
that you recommend them
outside of your company.

00:08:31.651 --> 00:08:33.346
Maybe the best thing for them to do

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:35.130
is not be a part of your company.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:37.570
So example, when people
call in to us to say,

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:39.569
hey, do you have a kids program?

00:08:39.569 --> 00:08:41.948
Well we don't right now,
there is no kids program.

00:08:41.948 --> 00:08:43.226
It's something that we've thought about,

00:08:43.226 --> 00:08:44.943
we're looking into, but
it's not a highest priority

00:08:44.943 --> 00:08:46.189
right now for us.

00:08:46.189 --> 00:08:49.224
And so instead of just saying
no it could also be okay,

00:08:49.224 --> 00:08:50.822
here are some options.

00:08:50.822 --> 00:08:52.338
If you get the question
enough you can look at

00:08:52.338 --> 00:08:53.171
different options.

00:08:53.171 --> 00:08:55.915
Here are some other schools
that provide kids programs.

00:08:55.915 --> 00:08:59.254
So maybe I'm sending my potential customer

00:08:59.254 --> 00:09:02.858
to one of my competitors but
it's the best thing for them.

00:09:02.858 --> 00:09:03.867
And they'll remember it.

00:09:03.867 --> 00:09:06.776
It's not often that that happens that

00:09:06.776 --> 00:09:10.670
a companies willing to recommend
you to their competition.

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.547
And whether you want to
take that bold step or not

00:09:12.547 --> 00:09:15.108
I can guarantee you that
it net net wins for you

00:09:15.108 --> 00:09:17.194
because they remember that relationship.

00:09:17.194 --> 00:09:19.808
And if they have another
potential option or question

00:09:19.808 --> 00:09:21.536
they're going to come back to you.

00:09:21.536 --> 00:09:24.269
But even if you don't recommend
off to a competing product

00:09:24.269 --> 00:09:27.011
just be able to recommend
the right thing for them,

00:09:27.011 --> 00:09:30.301
not just the thing that
you're trying to sell more of.

00:09:30.301 --> 00:09:32.283
So a great example a
buddy of mine named Louis

00:09:32.283 --> 00:09:33.976
runs a company called
Last Minute Training.

00:09:33.976 --> 00:09:36.250
They sell all sorts of different training.

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.270
So example, if you want to learn Excel

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:40.824
he'll put you into
different Excel classes.

00:09:40.824 --> 00:09:44.574
He knows which Excel classes
best fit for the customer

00:09:44.574 --> 00:09:45.993
but he also knows the ones
that are going to make him

00:09:45.993 --> 00:09:47.217
the most money.

00:09:47.217 --> 00:09:49.608
He will always do the best
thing for the customer

00:09:49.608 --> 00:09:52.260
even if he's going to make
more money off of this course

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:53.553
and send them on this day

00:09:53.553 --> 00:09:56.010
but he knows it doesn't
quite fit their criteria.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:58.209
He doesn't doesn't quite
give them what they want

00:09:58.209 --> 00:10:00.307
